1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,218
At 12:15 AM on September 26,

2
00:00:02,298 --> 00:00:08,129
1983, a red siren illuminated a top-secret Soviet bunker outside Moscow.

3
00:00:08,209 --> 00:00:12,644
The radar screens confirmed what every officer dreaded:

4
00:00:12,724 --> 00:00:17,160
five American nuclear warheads were already in the air.

5
00:00:17,239 --> 00:00:29,940
Soviet protocol gave Lieutenant Colonel Stanislav Petrov exactly twenty minutes to authorize a retaliatory strike that would wipe three hundred million people off the face of the Earth.

6
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:33,049
(pausa: 2s) The machine demanded retaliation.

7
00:00:33,129 --> 00:00:36,780
The satellite algorithms swore the missiles were real.

8
00:00:36,859 --> 00:00:39,658
He had a direct line to the Kremlin.

9
00:00:39,738 --> 00:00:43,496
His finger hovered over the confirmation switch.

10
00:00:43,576 --> 00:00:46,055
But instead of following orders.

11
00:00:46,135 --> 00:00:49,573
(pausa: 2s) Petrov decided to trust a hunch.

12
00:00:49,653 --> 00:00:54,051
If the United States was going to start World War Three.

13
00:00:54,131 --> 00:00:56,370
why send only five missiles?.
